: "dec", "n": 16}, {"chinese": "\u82e5\u70b9 P(x,2) \u662f\u89d2 \u03b1 \u7ec8\u8fb9\u4e0a\u7684\u70b9\uff0c\u4e14 tan \u03b1 = -1\uff0c\u5219 y =", "english": "If point P(x,2) is on the terminal side of angle \u03b1, and tan \u03b1 = -1, then y =", "options": ["A. 1", "B. 2", "C. -2", "D. -1"], "answer": "C", "topic": "trigonometry (simple)"}, {"chinese": "\u5df2\u77e5 sin \u03b1 = 3/5\uff0c\u4e14 \u03b1 \u662f\u7b2c\u4e8c\u8c61\u9650\u89d2\uff0c\u5219 cos \u03b1 =", "english": "Given that sin \u03b1 = 3/5, and \u03b1 is in the second quadrant, then cos \u03b1 =", "options": ["A. 4/5", "B. -4/5", "C. 3/4", "D. -3/4"], "answer": "B", "topic": "trigonometry (simple)", "type": "dec", "link": "https://t.me/c/3305923058/270", "n": 19}, {"chinese": "\u82e5 \u03b1 \u4e3a\u9510\u89d2\uff0c\u4e14sin \u03b1 = \u221a3/2\uff0c\u5219 tan \u03b1 =", "english": "If \u03b1 is an acute angle, and sin \u03b1 = \u221a3/2, then tan \u03b1 =", "options": ["A. 1/2", "B. \u221a3", "C. 1/4", "D. \u221a3/3"], "answer": "B", "topic": "trigonometry (simple)", "type": "dec", "link": "https://t.me/c/3305923058/274", "n": 22}, {"chinese": "\u5df2\u77e5 cos a = -1/2, \u03b1\u2208(\u03c0/2, \u03c0), \u5219 sin \u03b1 \u7684\u503c\u662f", "english": "Given that cos a = -1/2, \u03b1\u2208(\u03c0/2, \u03c0), then the value of sin \u03b1 is", "options": ["A. -\u221a3/2", "B. \u221a3/2", "C. 1/2", "D. -1/2"], "answer": "B", "link": "https://t.me/c/3305923058/282", "topic": "trigonometry (simple)", "type": "dec", "n": 34}, {"chinese": "\u5df2\u77e5\u89d2 \u03b1 = 5\u03c0/6\uff0c\u5219\u4e0b\u5217\u7ed3\u8bba\u6b63\u786e\u7684\u662f", "english": "Given angle \u03b1 = 5\u03c0/6, which conclusion is correct?", "options": ["A. sin \u03b1 = 1/2", "B. sin \u03b1 = -1/2", "C. sin \u03b1 = -\u221a3/2", "D. sin \u03b1 = \u221a3/2"], "answer": "A", "topic": "trigonometry (simple)", "subtopic": "trigonometric values", "type": "oct", "n": 6}, {"chinese": "\u5df2\u77e5\u89d2 \u03b1 = 5\u03c0/3\uff0c\u5219\u4e0b\u5217\u7ed3\u8bba\u6b63\u786e\u7684\u662f", "english": "Given angle \u03b1 = 5\u03c0/3, which conclusion is correct?", "options": ["A. sin \u03b1 = -1/2", "B. sin \u03b1 = 1/2", "C. cos \u03b1 = 1/2", "D. cos \u03b1 = -1/2"], "answer": "C", "topic": "trigonometry (simple)"}, {"chinese": "\u5df2\u77e5\u89d2 \u03b1 = 5\u03c0/4\uff0c\u5219\u4e0b\u5217\u7ed3\u8bba\u6b63\u786e\u7684\u662f", "english": "Given angle \u03b1 = 5\u03c0/4, which conclusion is correct?", "options": ["A. sin \u03b1 = -1/2", "B. sin \u03b1 = 1/2", "C. tan \u03b1 = 1", "D. tan \u03b1 = -1"], "answer": "D", "topic": "trigonometry (simple)"}, {"chinese": "\u5047\u8bbe\u4e00\u4e2a\u89d2 \u03b1 = 30\u00b0\u3002\u90a3\u4e48\u4e0b\u5217\u54ea\u4e2a\u9648\u8ff0\u662f\u6b63\u786e\u7684\uff1f\uff08 \uff09\u3002", "english": "Suppose that an angle \u03b1 = 30\u00b0. Then which of the following statements is correct? ( ).", "options": ["A. sin \u03b1 = \u221a2/2", "B. cos \u03b1 = \u221a3/2", "C. cos \u03b1 = 1/2", "D. tan \u03b1 = \u221a3"], "answer": "B", "topic": "trigonometry (simple)", "type": "jan", "n": 7}, {"chinese": "\u5df2\u77e5 sin \u03b1 = 4/5\uff0c\u5e76\u4e14\u89d2 \u03b1 \u5c5e\u4e8e\u7b2c\u4e8c\u8c61\u9650\uff0c\u90a3\u4e48\u4e0b\u5217\u54ea\u4e2a\u9648\u8ff0\u662f\u6b63\u786e\u7684\uff1f\uff08 \uff09", "english": "Given that sin \u03b1 = 4/5, and the angle \u03b1 belongs to the second quadrant, then which of the following statements is correct? ( )", "options": ["A. cos \u03b1 = 3/5", "B. cos \u03b1 = -3/5", "C. tan \u03b1 = -3/4", "D. tan \u03b1 = 4/3"], "answer": "B", "topic": "trigonometry (simple)", "type": "jan", "n": 20}]